---
import { site } from '../../data/site';

interface Props {
  /** `h1` on the standalone page, `h2` inside the dialog. */
  heading?: 'h1' | 'h2';
}

const { heading: Heading = 'h2' } = Astro.props;
/** Section headings sit one level below the title: h2 on the standalone page, h3 in the dialog. */
const Sub = Heading === 'h1' ? 'h2' : 'h3';
---

<Heading class="legal-title" id="privacy-title">Privacy</Heading>
<p>
  Protecting your personal data matters to me. I process data solely on the basis of the applicable law (GDPR, the
  Austrian Data Protection Act DSG and the Telecommunications Act TKG 2021).
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Controller</Sub>
<p>
  {site.name}, {site.residence}, East Tyrol, Austria<br />
  E-mail: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Hosting</Sub>
<p>
  This website runs on a server provided by netcup GmbH, Karlsruhe, Germany, acting as a processor. The server keeps no
  access logs. Technical error messages from the server may contain an IP address; they are stored only in small
  amounts and continuously overwritten. The legal basis is the legitimate interest in running the site securely and
  reliably (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Cloudflare</Sub>
<p>
  All requests to this website pass through the network of Cloudflare, Inc., San Francisco, USA (reverse proxy and
  content delivery network). Cloudflare processes technically necessary data such as your IP address, the page
  requested, date and time and browser information in order to deliver the website and protect it from attacks. The
  legal basis is the legitimate interest in secure and fast delivery (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare acts as a
  processor.
</p>
<p>
  Data may be transferred to the USA in the process. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework; the
  transfer is based on the European Commission's adequacy decision (Art. 45 GDPR) and, in addition, on standard
  contractual clauses. Cloudflare keeps this data only as long as necessary for delivery and security; details on the
  retention period are given in Cloudflare's privacy policy:
  <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Contact by e-mail</Sub>
<p>
  If you contact me by e-mail, the details you provide are stored to handle your enquiry and any follow-up questions
  (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). I delete them once your enquiry has been dealt with, unless a statutory retention obligation
  applies. I do not pass this data on without your consent.
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Cookies and local storage</Sub>
<p>
  This website sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser (§ 165(3) TKG 2021), so no consent is requested.
  There are no tracking or marketing services and no analytics tools.
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Fonts, scripts and images</Sub>
<p>
  All fonts, scripts and images are loaded from this domain. Apart from delivery via Cloudflare (see above), opening
  the website does not create a connection to Google or any other third party.
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">External links</Sub>
<p>
  Some project pages link to external websites. Data is only transferred to the respective operator once you click such
  a link; their privacy policy applies there.
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Project screenshots</Sub>
<p>
  The accounts, names and content visible in the screenshots of the web apps are fictional demo data. No data of real
  users is shown. The screenshots of the Musikkapelle Nikolsdorf website show members of the band as they appear on the
  club's public website and are used with permission.
</p>

<Sub class="legal-sub">Your rights</Sub>
<p>
  You have the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and data portability. You can object
  at any time to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21 GDPR). To exercise these rights, simply send me an
  e-mail. No automated decision-making or profiling takes place.
</p>
<p>
  If you believe that the processing of your data violates data protection law, you can lodge a complaint with the
  supervisory authority: Austrian Data Protection Authority (Österreichische Datenschutzbehörde), Barichgasse 40–42,
  1030 Vienna, <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.dsb.gv.at</a>
</p>

<p>Last updated: November 2026</p>
